# K03 NS-ROLES-2 REQUIRED POSITIVE, red until its dependency is built (Codex K03-NS2-COVERAGE-20261007-21;
# steps/defects.md#reference-field-consumers).
# `return: h\p` with Holder's p the binding `p: Eq` returns the Structure p references, Eq itself, admitted to the
# result Equatable; take's write through the returned reference reaches Eq.  Today: "a field path must end at a
# Structure" (unit_s7_ret_path keeps its admission refusal with an owned nested field).  Exit 7; 81 for a wrong result,
# 82 if the write did not reach Eq.
Equatable:
    size_t: equals 0U
end: Equatable
Eq:
    size_t: equals 0U
end: Eq
Holder:
    p: Eq
end: Holder
fn: pick (Holder: h) Equatable
    return: h\p
end: pick
fn: take (Equatable: slot) size_t
    slot\equals: 9U
    return: slot\equals
end: take
fn: m () int
    if: take(pick(Holder)) != 9U
        return: 81
    if: Eq\equals != 9U
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
